    <string name="background_hint_ok">Android lets MqttABot keep its connection open in the background.</string>
    <string name="background_hint_limited">Android may pause the subscription service in the background, so messages and Tasker events can be missed.</string>
    <string name="action_allow_background">Allow unrestricted</string>
    <string name="rationale_notifications_title">Notifications are off</string>
    <string name="rationale_notifications">While the subscription service runs, MqttABot shows an ongoing notification with the connection status and a Stop button. The service keeps running without it, but you won\'t see its status. You can turn notifications on in settings.</string>
    <string name="rationale_background_title">Background activity is limited</string>
    <string name="rationale_background">To receive MQTT messages and trigger Tasker while the screen is off, MqttABot keeps a connection open in the background. With battery optimization Android may cut that connection. In settings, set MqttABot\'s battery usage to Unrestricted.</string>
